    "ten_fragment_scope_differences": [
      {
        "source_item_id": "S2.Thmtheorem1",
        "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
        "kind": "theorem-proposition-corollary-container",
        "node_id": null,
        "reason": "Whole numbered/composite result is not the sealed partial conditional-variance slice; retained individual relevant items are inventoried separately.",
        "independent_outer_HTML_sha256": "72cd924958c7284c256bb467463abdb3f9590f4f0d31e51d852f49345e0f5aa0",
        "draft_fragment_sha256": "b1b8a0a14192c2b4891bb0a2164ec57c7122bd30bdfe9cfbb02fba5aeeda6740",
        "fragment_matches_full_canonical_element": false,
        "raw_start_char": 107823,
        "raw_end_char": 121216,
        "primary_text": "Proposition 2.1 (Geometry of the joint law) . The joint law ( 2.6 ) has the following properties. (i) For every y\\in\\mathbb{R}^{d} , the conditional law \\pi_{\\eta}^{X\\mid Y=y} has potential (that is, negative log-density up to an additive constant) V_{y}(x)\\coloneqq V(x)+\\frac{\\|x-y\\|^{2}}{2\\eta}\\,. (2.9) This conditional potential satisfies (\\alpha+\\eta^{-1})I\\preceq\\nabla^{2}V_{y}(x)\\preceq(\\beta+\\eta^{-1})I\\,, (2.10) so its condition number is at most (1+\\beta\\eta)/(1+\\alpha\\eta)\\leq 2 . Consequently, for every smooth f , \\Var_{\\pi_{\\eta}^{X\\mid Y=y}}(f)\\leq\\frac{\\eta}{1+\\alpha\\eta}\\,\\mathbb{E}_{\\pi_{\\eta}^{X\\mid Y=y}}\\|\\nabla f\\|^{2}\\,, (2.11) and \\frac{\\eta}{1+\\beta\\eta}I\\preceq\\mathrm{Cov}_{\\pi_{\\eta}^{X\\mid Y=y}}(X)\\preceq\\frac{\\eta}{1+\\alpha\\eta}I\\,. (2.12) (ii) The Y -marginal potential satisfies \\frac{\\alpha}{1+\\alpha\\eta}I\\preceq\\nabla^{2}U_{\\eta}(y)\\preceq\\frac{\\beta}{1+\\beta\\eta}I\\,. (2.13) (iii) The state-space reflection \\mathsf{U}:(x,y)\\mapsto(x,2x-y) (2.14) preserves \\pi_{\\eta} and is an involution."
      },
      {
        "source_item_id": "S2.Thmtheorem2",
        "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
        "kind": "theorem-proposition-corollary-container",
        "node_id": null,
        "reason": "Whole numbered/composite result is not the sealed partial conditional-variance slice; retained individual relevant items are inventoried separately.",
        "independent_outer_HTML_sha256": "b82308ccee23ff7825c21760f156e93eeb18fb57a71ab5b4290d4c4f854613a7",
        "draft_fragment_sha256": "61556b2012369a0cd21e8699c272bcfc01dd9ce4c93b0b55c8e4e489f9b214ca",
        "fragment_matches_full_canonical_element": false,
        "raw_start_char": 128056,
        "raw_end_char": 129560,
        "primary_text": "Definition 2.2 (Restricted Gaussian oracle) . For \\eta>0 , a restricted Gaussian oracle (RGO) takes input y\\in\\mathbb{R}^{d} and, using fresh randomness, returns a sample with law \\pi_{\\eta}^{X\\mid Y=y} ."
      },
